findings.claim:
The generic formal K-theory of Zhang's Appendix B has two owners in accepted routes. Its content is:
- K_0^Y and K′_0 of locally noetherian formal schemes;
- the codimension filtration;
- the regular comparison K_0^Y(X) ≅ K′_0(Y);
- derived intersections;
- the Euler characteristic χ(X, F ⊗^L G).
Route 10 sends it to 'K-theory of schemes, localisation and operations, Part II' (queued as SchemeKTheoryOperationsPartII). PAPER-LI-ZHANG-22-B's accepted route 2 has the Kudla–Rapoport Part II (queued as GrossZagierAndArithmeticHeightsPartII) construct the same objects. Its missing item PAPER-LI-ZHANG-22-B/46 is routed there, and so is the K_0^Y part of PAPER-HE-LI-SHI-ETAL-23/9. The two Part IIs are separate design jobs, so this material would be planned twice. Route 10's reason says the cycle briefs carry only 'unexpanded generic AppendixB placeholders'. That is not so: PAPER-LI-ZHANG-22-B/46 states the objects in full. Route 11's brief also keeps the duplicate obligation, since it says 'Retain the existing UnitaryKudlaRapoportCycles obligations'. Coordinator note: this session wrote RT-PAPER-HE-LI-SHI-ETAL-23 (PR #4957); its item 9 is cited only as the second duplicate. Severity set to medium by the coordinator: this extraction already makes route 10 the owner (route 10's reason) and route 11's brief already imports from it; what remains is the wording of route 11's brief and the other extractions' routing, as for the single-owner duplicates graded medium in RT-PAPER-FINTZEN-21. Also: Appendix B's formal supported K-theory is planned twice. Route 10 proposes FormalSupportedIntersections as its single owner. The accepted extraction PAPER-LI-ZHANG-22-B still routes the same material to UnitaryKudlaRapoportCycles: its item 46, 'K-theory with supports on formal schemes' (Zhang (B.1)–(B.3)). The UnitaryKudlaRapoportCycles brief there says to construct it. PAPER-LI-LIU-22/29 likewise routes formal K-classes citing Zhang App. B to UnitaryKudlaRapoportCycles. The extraction says the obligation 'is factored into a common supplier, not duplicated', but it names neither duplicate item. Nothing re-routes them, so two design jobs are told to build the same groups and filtrations. Moreover, PAPER-LI-ZHANG-22-B/46 asserts the formal-scheme (B.3), which this extraction treats a